course: dictionary
lesson: 4515
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «clashes heads going for a header» tells you a player is jumping for the ball. A header in football means hitting the ball with your head, not with your foot.
explain: The same word can mean something very different on a page. On a document, the header is the text at the top, such as the title or page number. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A noun names a thing. Header is a noun: a header, two headers.
fact: In football, a header is hitting the ball with your head.
fact: On a page, the header is the text at the top, such as the title or page number.
fact: In a computer file or email, the header holds information about it, such as the sender.
fact: In UK informal talk, «take a header» means to fall head first.
exercise: In the sentence «clashes heads going for a header», what does header mean? | The first part of a computer file | Text at the top of every page | *Hitting the ball with your head | A fall head first
exercise: Where would you write the title of a document so that it is seen on every page? | At the very end of the last page | In a bag | *In the header, at the top of the page | In the middle of the page
exercise: Read «take a header». What does it mean in informal UK talk? | *A fall head first | A kind of hat | A goal scored in football | A tidy plan
test: In a computer email, what does the header show? | *Information about the email, such as who sent it | Only the last line of the message | The spelling mistakes | A picture of the sender
test: Which phrase means scoring a goal by hitting the ball with your head? | «header and footer» | «take a dive» | «sit them out» | *«score with a header»
exam: Freya says «Howay, I'm fine man, let's gan». What does gan mean? | Eat | Stop | Sit | *Go
